Fix RSA keys with public exponent 1, which Fusion 360 imports.

Wine 11.11 moved rsaenh from libtomcrypt to SymCrypt. Fusion 360 imports a
512-bit RSA private key whose public exponent is 1; with e == 1 both RSA
operations are the identity (m^1 mod n == m), which libtomcrypt handled but
SymCrypt rejected, so CryptImportKey failed and Fusion's 3D subsystem never
initialised - the 3D canvas stayed black while the Qt interface worked.

Wine commit 0cb249ce ("symcrypt: Accept RSA keys with public exponent 1")
only commented out the guard in SymCryptRsakeyCalculatePrivateFields(). The
import succeeds since then, but SymCryptIntExtendedGcd() computes the inverse
as -((B1*Src1 - Gcd)/Src2) mod Src1, which does not hold for Src2 == 1, so the
derived private exponent and both CRT exponents are wrong. The public
operation is correct, the private one is not, and the canvas stays black.

The inverse of 1 is 1, so set the private exponent directly; the CRT loop
below then derives dp = dq = 1 as it should.

diff --git a/libs/symcrypt/lib/rsakey.c b/libs/symcrypt/lib/rsakey.c
--- a/libs/symcrypt/lib/rsakey.c
+++ b/libs/symcrypt/lib/rsakey.c
@@ -423,6 +423,15 @@ SymCryptRsakeyCalculatePrivateFields(
             goto cleanup;
         }

+        // IntExtendedGcd computes the inverse as -((B1*Src1 - Gcd)/Src2) mod Src1,
+        // which does not hold for Src2 == 1. The inverse of 1 is 1, so set it
+        // directly; the CRT exponents derived below then come out as 1 as well.
+        if( pkRsakey->au64PubExp[i] == 1 )
+        {
+            SymCryptIntSetValueUint32( 1, pkRsakey->piPrivExps[i] );
+            continue;
+        }
+
         // Calculate D
         SymCryptIntSetValueUint64( pkRsakey->au64PubExp[i], piScr );

